o down the path of  body doubles or surgical manipulation or  anything but there is the possibility  that the man who died on the dock wasn't  actually the man himself  i mean our agents have never actually  met kina face to face  agents that had either joined him or  were killed we've only heard from  through recordings and grainy videos and  echoes which to be fair he looked quite  different in a number of them  however before i get too crazy with all  this and start digging down into  conspiracy theories let's jump back into  the story  before we landed on liberty island we  confronted kina's rogue agents one of  them being theo parnell  theo was a tech genius and while we were  actively hunting him down he proved time  and time again that isaac couldn't be  trusted he showed how easy it was to  manipulate the ai into doing reporting  and saying whatever he wanted it to  this is a big part of how theo's special  tech the decoy works  following on from theo's death kina or  whoever we were fighting showed again  how easy it was to control isaac by  having it relay anything he wanted it to  straight into our earpieces  it's entirely possible that theo and  kina had orchestrated the whole plan  that we the agents were meant to catch  up with keener on the island and take  him down or at least think we had  so what was the point in faking his  death  to buy himself some time  similar to what he did on the west side  piers to create a distraction while he  continued on with his plans  except through having everyone think  that he was dead the division and the  black tusk would no longer be looking  for him turning their complete attention  on each other  perhaps things were getting a little too  hot for him after his portrayal of the  black tusk and this was his contingency  plan to get the heat off his back  and the only other person that knew of  this  was theo which is why keanu was happy to  let him die at the hands of the division  from here keena may be continuing to  build his network of rogues  when you think about it we've only  really met so many so far  there are likely hundreds if not  thousands more of them out there  don't get me wrong i'm not really a fan  of the whole surprise he isn't dead idea  but i certainly wouldn't be upset if  keena comes back into the picture he was  definitely one of the more interesting  characters of the story  and this could actually help us  understand the unusual direction his  character talk at the end there  but if they do go down this path they  have to do it right because personally  and i know for a lot of others this  could break the immersion of the story  if it was done half-assed  there are a number of holes in the story  that would need to be plugged in order  to have this work  i touched on this a while ago but having  gone through it again recently i still  think it has merit and would still  probably be my preferred direction that  the story could take though certainly  not the most likely  at the end of the fellow manhunt  everything just stopped  we didn't get a cut scene there wasn't  some epic yet strangely concerning  speech from kalso or paul rhodes we  didn't even receive a notification from  isaac to say that she was deceased or  eliminated  obviously the whole ending to this  manhunt was pretty disappointing but the  sudden announcement from the division  development team that went on to explain  this manhunt was originally meant to be  the last major update to the game could  be the reason that we were left hanging  after taking down fae  i believe that there was meant to be  more to the story but because the game  was now suddenly being built on again  they changed how it was going to play  out  what if we were supposed to capture faye  similar to what we did with schaefer but  due to the apparent unexpected decision  to extend on the division over the next  year or so they potentially cut out the  final cinematic to be expanded on later  faye locates prison 