en burned likely now to be flagged as  a rogue organization  but as there are so few of them left and  the fact that they're only losing ground  to this invading force  it was a sacrifice she had to make  plus she's likely come to the conclusion  that she can't do this alone  through doing this she may be able to  bring more of them undercover into the  btsu to help with the mission  feylau decided that it was up to her to  do what no division agent was able to  and that the only way to do this was to  go rogue and join up with the black tusk  taking down alice and the rest of its  leadership from the inside  faye had no problems with the fact that  she could die while on this mission  other than taking a chance and  eliminating the leadership i don't think  she had planned her next steps and was  forced to make some quick decisions on  the fly including the blaming of alice's  murder  and she certainly wasn't expecting to be  captured alive by the division  due to the shd now being labeled as  hostile there is the potential for a  little bit of a rift between the jtf and  the division  fey has been held in an undisclosed  location where she has been interrogated  by an understandably angry ilani calso  given kauso's generally less flexible  demeanor faye takes the beating and says  nothing  she has a plan but it involves keeping  the undercover situation on a need to  know basis  all faye says is that she wants to talk  to  benitez eventually kelso organizes a  meet-up with benitez  although he is jtf he knows faye better  than anyone else  if anyone's going to get her to talk  it's him  faye tells them everything and that this  is far bigger that they could have ever  planned for  but she isn't done and she needs his  help to finish the job  benitez believes her and on top of this  provides her with the means to escape  at this stage the btsu has no idea that  she's been captured but she couldn't  simply walk back in and join the black  tusk ranks after disappearing for so  long  she needed something that would not only  lower the chances of questions being  raised but something that would bolster  her position into the leadership  benitez further assists by providing the  location and guard schedule of  baden-schaefer  he would be a ticket back in  after breaking barton free faye rejoins  with the black tusk  although natalia sokolova is still  skeptical faye's position within the  organization has been somewhat elevated  however she is quickly put to the test  council has brought in a number of  agents to recapture faye and schaefer  she launches an assault on faye's last  known location where they once again  meet face to face  the following weeks see a number of  conflicts between faye and kelso  over time more agents are brought into  phase circle and are made aware of her  plans  but kelso is a stubbornly loyal  individual she fights for what she  believes is right  all she sees is an agent who is in a  once prominent position turning her back  on the people  the conflict continues  but now the battle is between rogue  agents fighting for different sides  in time castle would come on board with  the plan  and from here they were able to  orchestrate a number of skirmishes that  would solidify faye's position  together calso and fey would effectively  control the black tusk operations  one from the opposing side keeping up  the illusion and the other from within  their ranks  with every conflict faye gains more  trust from sokolova  she would advise kelso on opportunities  to discover intel and break convoy lines  yet faye would be able to continue  taking locations of interest for circle  over while keeping collateral damage to  a  minimum over time they would be able to  work towards bringing down natalia's  organization  including her potentially secret force  of super soldiers  the hunters  as much as i'd like to see these ideas  become the future direction of the game  we need to think about what we've seen  from t